&lt;div&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;ABOUT THE ROLE&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anduril’s Space Manufacturing team is seeking a Lead Manufacturing Engineer to join our team. Your expertise will help ensure that our products meet the highest standards of quality and reliability at Anduril.&amp;nbsp;As the Lead Manufacturing Engineer, you will be a technical leader responsible for owning the manufacturing strategy and execution for complex spacecraft hardware.Our team&#39;s scope encompasses&amp;nbsp;the entire vehicle integration value chain, including Design for Manufacturability, advanced manufacturing process development, tooling design &amp;amp; selection, supplier technical management, quality system implementation, and comprehensive work documentation. You will lead cross-functional initiatives, mentor junior engineers, and&amp;nbsp;drive excellence across our products&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The ideal candidate demonstrates proven leadership in solving complex technical challenges with innovative, practical solutions in fast-paced, resource-constrained environments. You have successfully scaled manufacturing processes from prototype through production and have a track record of delivering high-reliability hardware on aggressive timelines.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;br&gt;WHAT YOU’LL DO&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Degree in a technical field such as engineering, math, or a hard science.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years in manufacturing or similar prototyping position.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years as a SME in either Sensors and Avionics, Vehicle Integration, or Propulsion and Energetics&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated in-kind or direct team leadership skills, with backing examples.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An attitude of world-class mission assurance, quality, attention to detail, and dedication.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A genuine interest in manufacturing and thirst for learning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to creatively deliver hardware in a resource-constrained environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Personal experience physically manufacturing hardware via any means (machining, fabrication, soldering, assembly, etc.). Work on personal or extracurricular projects is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be a U.S. Person due to required access to U.S. export-controlled information or facilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Mechanical, Aerospace, Manufacturing or Industrial Engineering, or a related technical discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years designing production tooling, fixtures or mechanical ground support equipment for aerospace, space, defense or another high-reliability industry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A portfolio of tooling or MGSE personally designed and saw through to released drawings, fabrication and use on the floor&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong CAD proficiency (NX, SolidWorks or CREO) with sound GD&amp;amp;T practice on tooling drawings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Structural sizing and load path analysis experience for handling and lift hardware, including proof load and lift certification requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing tooling or MGSE that operated inside a cleanroom, and can defend the material, coating and lubricant choices that made it acceptable. Familiarity with IEST-STD-CC1246 and ASTM E595.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience specifying and procuring tooling or capital equipment through a supply chain — specifications, vendor selection, long-lead planning and acceptance — against a facility or program schedule.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A quantified improvement delivered through tooling or automation — cycle time, ergonomic risk, defect rate or touch labor — that you can explain mechanically.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to obtain and maintain an active U.S. Secret security clearance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel up to 25%&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years designing production tooling, fixtures or mechanical ground support equipment for aerospace, space, defense or another high-reliability industry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or transforming successful production operation organizations and leading large-scale change management initiatives that influence culture, define tools &amp;amp; processes and improve competencies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cleanroom manufacturing experience, or equivalent work in another contamination-controlled environment, with contamination control and FOD prevention discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on fluency with a manufacturing execution system and a PLM system as the system of record — build definition, work instruction or work order authoring, as-built records and production data. Teamcenter, SAP, Windchill or equivalent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success in scaling product testing and production from single units to hundreds per year.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading and managing teams on fast-paced, complex projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Skills in cost analysis, cost reduction strategies, and managing production budgets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with software &amp;amp; firmware flashing or end-of-line testing &amp;amp; troubleshooting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Software scripting experience in any language.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Eligible to obtain and maintain an active U.S. Top Secret security clearance&lt;/li&gt;
