&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Anduril Industries is a defense technology company with a mission to transform U.S. and allied military capabilities with advanced technology. By bringing the expertise, technology, and business model of the 21st century’s most innovative companies to the defense industry, Anduril is changing how military systems are designed, built and sold. Anduril’s family of systems is powered by Lattice OS, an AI-powered operating system that turns thousands of data streams into a realtime, 3D command and control center. As the world enters an era of strategic competition, Anduril is committed to bringing cutting-edge autonomy, AI, computer vision, sensor fusion, and networking technology to the military in months, not years.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT THE TEAM&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anduril’s Rocket Motor Systems team is seeking a Equipment Safety Engineer III to join our team. The Rocket Motor Systems team is designing and commissioning automated equipment for high rate production of Solid Rocket Motors at our plant in McHenry, MS. In this role, you will help to ensure automation equipment is designed, validated, and operated to the highest safety standards.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU’LL DO&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support machine safety efforts for manufacturing &amp;amp; process equipment at Anduril’s Solid Rocket Motor production facility in McHenry, MS&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a safety resource during design, commissioning, and validation of automated / semi-automated production equipment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct hazard analysis / risk assessments and support safety buyoff for equipment including conveyance, robotics, process equipment, and lifting systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Specify and validate safety systems including E-Stops, scanners, light curtains, door interlocks, and other relevant hardware&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigate and provide corrective actions for equipment safety failures or workplace injuries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure regulatory compliance for production equipment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Robotics/Controls, Mechanical Engineering, Electrical Engineering, Manufacturing Engineering, or similar&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of machine safety experience in a production environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of selection, integration, and validation of safety hardware&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiar with machine safety standards such as ISO 12100, ISO 13849, and ANSI B11&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiar with CAD packages including NX, Solidworks, or AutoCAD&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be a U.S. Person due to required access to U.S. export controlled information or facilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of machine safety experience in a production environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Functional Safety certification (TUV Rheinland, TUV SUD, or CMSE [TUV NORD]), or willingness to obtain one&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with control panel layout, electrical component selection, and cable routing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience interfacing with regulatory agencies and safety committees&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with energetic or other highly hazardous production processes&lt;/li&gt;
