&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;By submitting your application, you consent to Anduril Industries using a third-party service provider to conduct pre-employment risk, integrity, and due diligence screening and assessing potential risks as part of your application process. This third-party service provider provides risk-intelligence services that may include analysis of sanctions and watchlists, adverse media, public-record information, and other lawful open-source or commercial data sources. This third-party service provider does not act as a consumer reporting agency. Use of this provider helps to ensure compliance with applicable laws and protect technology, intellectual property, and organizational security.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Anduril Industries is a defense technology company with a mission to transform U.S. and allied military capabilities with advanced technology. By bringing the expertise, technology, and business model of the 21st century’s most innovative companies to the defense industry, Anduril is changing how military systems are designed, built and sold. Anduril’s family of systems is powered by Lattice OS, an AI-powered operating system that turns thousands of data streams into a realtime, 3D command and control center. As the world enters an era of strategic competition, Anduril is committed to bringing cutting-edge autonomy, AI, computer vision, sensor fusion, and networking technology to the military in months, not years.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;ABOUT THE TEAM&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Maneuver Dominance team at Anduril develops operationally relevant, multi-asset autonomy. Omen is Anduril’s hover-to-cruise autonomous air vehicle (AAV) that packs the endurance, payload, and mission flexibility of much larger airplanes into a novel runway-independent Group 3 platform. Omen can operate from ship decks, beaches, or remote island clearings, providing true runway independence and freedom of maneuver across defense and civilian domains. Omen is the first tail-sitter aircraft with a mass-production contract, with an order of 50 systems representing a decisive investment that anchors production and accelerates the development of future systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT THE JOB&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Formula SAE, Baja SAE, Design Build Fly, or an equivalent history of building things that move. We need a Mechatronics Engineer to own the integration of electromechanical actuation, sensing, and control subsystems that enable Omen&#39;s hover-to-cruise transition, ensuring every system, payload, and sensor interface performs reliably across the full flight envelope.&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;WHAT YOU&#39;LL DO&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bridge the software team and hardware teams, ensuring both teams are in alignment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own payload hardware integration end to end. EO/IR and imaging sensors, RF payloads, gimbals, rangefinders, inertial and position sensing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive mission system selection through trade studies balancing performance, SWaP, thermal, latency, and environmental robustness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Characterize sensors on the bench and in flight: noise, latency, bias and drift, boresight stability, and failure modes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and own payload interface control; mechanical mounting and alignment, power and signal definitions, harnessing, vehicle bus integration, and time synchronization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write production software and firmware for payload subsystems; drivers, sensor processing, pointing and stabilization control loops, calibration and coordinate frame libraries, health management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support aircraft integration, bring-up, and functional checkout, and plan and execute ground and flight test campaigns for payload performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead root-cause investigations for payload and pointing anomalies spanning mechanical, electrical, firmware, and software boundaries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Feed lessons learned back into ICDs, calibration procedures, and production assembly and acceptance test documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong engineering background from industry or school, ideally in Mechatronics, Robotics, Electrical Engineering, Aerospace, Computer Science, or Physics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of hands-on electromechanical and sensor integration experience in robotics, aerospace, or similar&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of C++ (or Rust) in a Linux environment, plus tooling in Python; demonstrated experience developing software for hardware&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency across a meaningful portion of the robotics stack, from sensor interfacing to actuation. Partial stack is okay&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid grasp of low-level communications (Ethernet, CAN, UART, SPI, I2C), real-time systems, and motor control&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with sensor characterization, calibration, and coordinate frame management; cameras, IMUs, encoders, GNSS, or LIDAR&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building and executing hardware test rigs, with competence on oscilloscopes, logic analyzers, DMMs, and test automation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to read schematics, support board bring-up, and define harnesses alongside EEs; familiarity with CAD (SolidWorks, NX, or equivalent)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High ownership and a bias toward action&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel 25% with potential surges above 25%&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Eligible to obtain and maintain an active U.S. Secret security clearance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;VTOL, tail-sitter, or rotorcraft experience, and familiarity with the payload environment they create (vibration, EMI, rotor wash)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with rapid payload/sensor integration onto unmanned platforms, including flight test support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with gimbals, stabilized pointing, boresighting, and geo-referencing or targeting chains&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in perception, localization, mapping, tracking, or guidance, and related system performance metrics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Embedded firmware in C, including device drivers and optimizing for limited resources&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with avionics buses (ARINC 429, MIL-STD-1553, Ethernet avionics) and time sync (PTP, PPS)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Modeling and controls in MATLAB/Simulink; experience building SIL/HIL simulators&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Environmental qualification testing experience (MIL-STD-810, MIL-STD-461) for electromechanical assemblies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience troubleshooting remotely deployed software on fielded hardware&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;US Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$146,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$194,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;The salary range for this role is an estimate based on a wide range of compensation factors, inclusive of base salary only. Actual salary offer may vary based on (but not limited to) work experience, education and/or training, critical skills, and/or business considerations. Highly competitive equity grants are included in the majority of full time offers; and are considered part of Anduril&#39;s total compensation package. Additionally, Anduril offers top-tier benefits for full-time employees, including:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;detailElios&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;At Anduril, we invest in our people. Our comprehensive, competitive benefits package (available at little to no cost to employees) ensures you’re supported in health, recovery, and whatever comes next.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;For more information, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.anduril.com/careers&quot;&gt;Explore Our Benefits&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;RichText column1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;detailElios&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Protecting Yourself from Recruitment Scams&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;detailElios&quot;&gt;Anduril is committed to maintaining the integrity of our Talent acquisition process and the security of our candidates. We&#39;ve observed a rise in sophisticated phishing and fraudulent schemes where individuals impersonate Anduril representatives, luring job seekers with false interviews or job offers. These scammers often attempt to extract payment or sensitive personal information.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;RichText column2&quot;&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;detailElios&quot;&gt;To ensure your safety and help you navigate your job search with confidence, please keep the following critical points in mind:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;detailElios&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;No Financial Requests:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Anduril will never solicit payment or demand personal financial details (such as banking information, credit card numbers, or social security numbers) at any stage of our hiring process. Our legitimate recruitment is entirely free for candidates.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Please always verify communications:&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct from Anduril: If you receive an email from one of our recruiters, it will &lt;em&gt;only&lt;/em&gt; come from an &lt;code&gt;@anduril.com&lt;/code&gt; address.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Via Agency Partner: If contacted by a recruiting agency for an Anduril role, their email will clearly identify their agency. If you suspect any suspicious activity, please verify the agency&#39;s authenticity by reaching out to &lt;a href=&quot;mailto:contact@anduril.com&quot;&gt;contact@anduril.com&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;detailElios&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Exercise Caution with Unsolicited Outreach:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;If you receive any communication that appears suspicious, contains grammatical errors, or makes unusual requests, do not engage. Always confirm the sender&#39;s email domain is @anduril.com before providing any personal information or clicking on links.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;detailElios&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What to Do If You Suspect Fraud:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Should you encounter any questionable or fraudulent outreach claiming to be from Anduril, please report it immediately to&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:contact@anduril.com&quot;&gt;contact@anduril.com&lt;/a&gt;. Your proactive caution is invaluable in protecting your personal information and upholding the security and trustworthiness of our recruitment efforts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Privacy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;To view Anduril&#39;s candidate data privacy policy, please visit &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-charstyle=&quot;Hyperlink&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://anduril.com/applicant-privacy-notice/&quot;&gt;https://anduril.com/applicant-privacy-notice/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;By submitting your application, you consent to Anduril Industries using a third-party service provider to conduct pre-employment risk, integrity, and due diligence screening and assessing potential risks as part of your application process. This third-party service provider provides risk-intelligence services that may include analysis of sanctions and watchlists, adverse media, public-record information, and other lawful open-source or commercial data sources. This third-party service provider does not act as a consumer reporting agency. Use of this provider helps to ensure compliance with applicable laws and protect technology, intellectual property, and organizational security.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Anduril Industries is a defense technology company with a mission to transform U.S. and allied military capabilities with advanced technology. By bringing the expertise, technology, and business model of the 21st century’s most innovative companies to the defense industry, Anduril is changing how military systems are designed, built and sold. Anduril’s family of systems is powered by Lattice OS, an AI-powered operating system that turns thousands of data streams into a realtime, 3D command and control center. As the world enters an era of strategic competition, Anduril is committed to bringing cutting-edge autonomy, AI, computer vision, sensor fusion, and networking technology to the military in months, not years.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT THE TEAM&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Connected Warfare division builds systems to support global command and control missions. We create joint, time-sensitive, multi-domain, ubiquitous, connected mesh ecosystems. Our ecosystem enables connected warfare with disproportional impact by connecting every robot, human, and sensor in every domain, bringing together hundreds of thousands of end points across the globe. We are the substrate that provides the source of truth for time-sensitive decisions, effectively transforming the way that militaries close kill chains and enable mission autonomy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Mission Operations (MOPs) team is responsible for managing the execution, growth, and success of our customer accounts. Working across product, engineering, sales, and logistics teams, our Mission Operations Engineers own the customer relationships and develop, plan, and deploy Anduril products in support of their missions. They work side-by-side with customers to understand their specific problem sets and then shape Anduril’s offerings alongside our engineering teams to fit the mission needs. Because the problems we solve are uniquely challenging, our Mission Operations Engineers naturally gravitate toward finding solutions and are adept at navigating organizational hurdles. They are ultimately responsible for customer and mission success and therefore play a critical role in the shaping and future of Anduril Industries.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT THE JOB&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Orchestrate the deployment of Anduril products.&lt;/strong&gt; Lead the planning, integration, and deployment of Anduril’s flagship software and hardware products in support of Army Intelligence missions. Through collaboration with our engineering, logistics, and technical operations teams, Mission Operators are in charge of deploying our products to customer environments, training end-users, and ensuring the high performance of our systems. We are obsessed with engagement and keeping our finger on the pulse of how customers interact with our systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Grow your business through programmatic success.&lt;/strong&gt; You will be responsible for defining, proposing, and executing programmatic and business strategies that drive technology adoption and scale Anduril&#39;s footprint within the Army Intelligence community. This requires establishing committed and trust-based partnerships with PMs and acquisition leaders to not only help them solve their immediate problems, but also to foresee future opportunities where Anduril’s technology can make them more effective.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shape our products to meet Army Intelligence workflows.&lt;/strong&gt; Work side-by-side with Army tactical and enterprise intelligence stakeholders to understand their workflows, system bottlenecks, and data integration needs. You will represent these users directly to Anduril&#39;s product and engineering teams, translating user feedback into actionable features on our product roadmaps.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborate across nearly every Anduril team.&lt;/strong&gt; Successfully deploying our complex systems requires collaborating with nearly every internal Anduril team - engineering, product, logistics, business development, contracting, and technical operations. You’ll be responsible for ensuring each party is engaged and informed, bringing the best of Anduril to the Aberdeen Proving Ground (APG) ecosystem.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT WE&#39;RE LOOKING FOR&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mission First Mindset.&lt;/strong&gt; We put the needs of the mission and our customers first. We actively seek out opportunities to better understand Army Intelligence workflows, with a goal to build the best possible products for the warfighter and radically evolve national defense capabilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ownership Mentality.&lt;/strong&gt; We’re looking for owners—those who have a natural bias to assume responsibility and contribute to a culture of performance. You will actively own the technical and programmatic relationships with key PEO IEW&amp;amp;S stakeholders, driving challenging and vague technical integration problems to clarity and resolution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Aptitude and Intellectual Curiosity.&lt;/strong&gt; We are first and foremost a technology company. You must be comfortable communicating complex technical concepts, understanding how modern software and hardware systems integrate, and getting hands-on in lab environments to configure and test systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Structured Thinker and Problem Solver.&lt;/strong&gt; Leading technical programs requires clear communication and well thought-out plans. We are looking for assertive communicators who can distill complex Army system-of-systems architectures into digestible integration plans.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;High Value Team Member.&lt;/strong&gt; At Anduril, the path to success weaves through the organization. We are a low-ego group that promotes teamwork and collaboration. You can develop rapport at both the tactical operator level and the executive/acquisition leadership level.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;360 Degree Leader.&lt;/strong&gt; We are a flat, non-hierarchical organization. We expect you to lead and influence people through both formal and informal constructs, identifying operational gaps and solving them immediately rather than stepping back.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU&#39;LL DO:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary technical and programmatic interface between Anduril Connected Warfare and the Army Intelligence community in the Aberdeen Proving Ground (APG) area, owning the relationship with the Army’s Capability Program Executive Intelligence and Spectrum Warfare (CPE ISW)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a deep understanding of Army Intelligence workflows and feed these insights directly into Anduril product roadmaps to ensure our capabilities support and enhance tactical intelligence missions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand connected systems (e.g., NGC2 and other modernized command and control/intelligence nodes) and shape technical integration approaches with the Army Intelligence community&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, propose, and execute creative programmatic and business approaches to expand Anduril’s integration and deployment across CPE ISW portfolios&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide hands-on, basic operational and technical integration support for Anduril hardware and software capabilities in both customer test beds and company laboratory environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design &amp;amp; implement user feedback loops to gather, triage, and prioritize requirements and integration hurdles discovered during lab testing, exercises, and field evaluations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Anduril’s software and hardware engineering teams to ensure our systems align with Army open architecture standards and interface guidelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep domain expertise within the U.S. Army Intelligence community, including familiarity with intelligence systems, workflows, and tactical operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience in technical program management, systems engineering, or technical account management roles within defense technology&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Army connected C2/Intel systems (such as NGC2, TITAN, or AIDP)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to support basic technical configuration, troubleshooting, and operation of software/hardware systems in lab environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interpersonal and stakeholder management skills, with a demonstrated ability to build trust with technical and non-technical military leaders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be located in, or willing to relocate to, the Aberdeen Proving Ground (APG), MD area&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel (25-50%)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must possess active SECRET clearance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience with the acquisition side of Army Intelligence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in Defense Technology Product Management, Solutions Architecture, or Technical Customer Success roles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with modern software development concepts (APIs, containerization, tactical cloud, and data fusion pipelines)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;US Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$167,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$209,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;The salary range for this role is an estimate based on a wide range of compensation factors, inclusive of base salary only. Actual salary offer may vary based on (but not limited to) work experience, education and/or training, critical skills, and/or business considerations. Highly competitive equity grants are included in the majority of full time offers; and are considered part of Anduril&#39;s total compensation package. Additionally, Anduril offers top-tier benefits for full-time employees, including:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;detailElios&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;At Anduril, we invest in our people. Our comprehensive, competitive benefits package (available at little to no cost to employees) ensures you’re supported in health, recovery, and whatever comes next.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;For more information, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.anduril.com/careers&quot;&gt;Explore Our Benefits&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
