&lt;p&gt;Applicants wishing to view a copy of SpaceX’s Affirmative Action Plan for veterans and individuals with disabilities, or applicants requiring reasonable accommodation to the application/interview process should reach out to&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:EEOCompliance@spacex.com&quot;&gt;EEOCompliance@spacex.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of&amp;nbsp;enabling human life on Mars.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Automation &amp;amp; Controls Engineer, Launch Hardware Production (Starship)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of enabling human life on Mars.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Automation &amp;amp; Controls Engineer, Launch Hardware Production (Starship)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role owns the controls that build Starship.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will design, commission, and operate the automation behind production systems. A 24-lane, 750,000 sq ft Starship Refurbishment facility (Gigabay) built to assemble &amp;amp; refurbish Starship at rate.&amp;nbsp;Industrial air separation units upstream of the propellant farms.&amp;nbsp;Heat shield tile manufacturing. This team owns that controls scope end to end.&amp;nbsp;The work runs from a blank cabinet and a P&amp;amp;ID to a plant that stays up. You will specify instrumentation, program PLCs, pull in the data, commission the equipment, and then live with it in production. When a lane stops, a cold box trips, or a furnace drifts, you find it, fix it, and change the system so it does not happen again.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position is based in Cape Canaveral, FL (Kennedy Space Center).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, build, and commission the controls for a 24-lane Gigabay: production tooling, lifts, fixtures, factory services, and the data layer the floor uses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring industrial air separation units online and keep them running. Own the instrumentation, interlocks, and control narratives for compression, cold box, distillation, storage, and transfer into the propellant farms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own controls for heat shield tile manufacturing: thermal process equipment, material handling, inspection, and the data that ties process settings to tile quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stand up new equipment from first power-on through rate production, then own uptime once it is live.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and upgrade data acquisition and control systems as the factory, the air separation plant, and the tile line change.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain the operational capability of control-voltage (&amp;lt;60V) electrical systems once activated.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn sensor and PLC data into something operators and responsible engineers can act on the same shift.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support controls technicians and the mechanical, facilities, and process engineers who depend on these systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design hardware and work methods that cut cost, install time, and the time it takes to recover a down line.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze data to judge the health of electrical and process systems, and use it to drive the next change.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in physics, electrical engineering, or computer engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ months of experience working with data acquisition systems (internship or project experience qualifies).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to design, implement, commission, and troubleshoot industrial control and data acquisition hardware.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on PLC and industrial network experience: Modbus, PROFINET, EtherNet/IP, or equivalent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience commissioning process or factory equipment and supporting it after it is in production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of instrumentation in classified and cryogenic service (NFPA 70, NFPA 70E; Class I, Division 1 and Division 2, or IEC equivalent).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fundamental understanding of the equipment behind a plant: sensors, valves, drives, analyzers, power distribution, grounding, and signal integrity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with mixed-signal electronics, schematic capture, and PCB design, verification, or validation where custom hardware is the right answer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;First-hand programming experience beyond ladder: enough software to move data out of a controller and into a tool the factory can use.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of high-reliability build, test, and documentation practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication. You will write the narrative, then go stand at the panel with the technician.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong work ethic, a bias for finishing, and the ability to change roles quickly in a high-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to drive work with incomplete information and to keep several systems moving at once.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for making the hardware that makes flight rate possible.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to pass an Air Force background check for Cape Canaveral.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to perform job duties that require standing, kneeling, crouching, twisting, and working in cramped positions and small openings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to climb stairs and ladders regularly throughout the day.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to lift lightweight supplies or materials (up to 25 lb unassisted).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Available to work extended hours and weekends when commissioning or production needs it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work performed around fumes, odors, flashing lights, heat, cold, and noise.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel to other SpaceX or third-party facilities (up to 25%).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ITAR REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;To conform to U.S. Government export regulations, applicant must be a (i) U.S. citizen or national, (ii) U.S. lawful, permanent resident (aka green card holder), (iii) Refugee under 8 U.S.C. § 1157, or (iv) Asylee under 8 U.S.C. § 1158, or be eligible to obtain the required authorizations from the U.S. Department of State. Learn more about the ITAR &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.pmddtc.state.gov/?id=ddtc_kb_article_page&amp;amp;sys_id=24d528fddbfc930044f9ff621f961987&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SpaceX is an Equal Opportunity Employer; employment with SpaceX is governed on the basis of merit, competence and qualifications and will not be influenced in any manner by race, color, religion, gender, national origin/ethnicity, veteran status, disability status, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, marital status, mental or physical disability or any other legally protected status.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Applicants wishing to view a copy of SpaceX’s Affirmative Action Plan for veterans and individuals with disabilities, or applicants requiring reasonable accommodation to the application/interview process should reach out to&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:EEOCompliance@spacex.com&quot;&gt;EEOCompliance@spacex.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of&amp;nbsp;enabling human life on Mars.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AUTOMATION &amp;amp; CONTROLS ENGINEER, LAUNCH PAD (STARSHIP)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SpaceX’s Starship spacecraft and Super Heavy rocket, collectively known as Starship, is a fully reusable transportation system designed to carry crew and cargo to Earth orbit, the Moon, Mars, and beyond. We are looking for an automation &amp;amp; controls engineer to develop and build launch and test systems for Starship, focusing on electrical control systems for the launch mount, integration tower, and orbital propellant farm, including input/output (I/O), motion systems, drive controls, and supporting infrastructure. The successful candidate will join a highly talented team of engineers with a proven track record of developing advanced automated solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Electrical systems:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architect, design, integrate, and commission control systems for the Starship launch pads&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design industrial electrical control panels that are National Fire Protection Association 79 (NFPA 79)/National Electrical Code (NEC)/Underwriters Laboratories 508A (UL 508A) compliant&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design control and data acquisition systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and author electrical schematics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design electrical conveyance and distribution systems (e.g., raceways, cables, wiring methods)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with other disciplines; interface control systems with high-power equipment and communication equipment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design electrical systems for hazardous environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Control software:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architect, write, and debug programmable logic controller (PLC) code with an emphasis on generating code that is organized, structured, documented, maintainable, and reusable for similar applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Configure, commission, and tune variable frequency drives (VFDs) for open- and closed-loop control system applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generate aesthetically simple human-machine interface (HMI) screens for complex machinery while providing sufficient feedback for troubleshooting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commission devices using a variety of industrial communication protocols&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set up and tune proportional-integral-derivative (PID) controllers for continuous processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Mechanical integration:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Add detail for electrical assemblies to computer-aided design (CAD) models to plan out installation for cable tray, conduit, panel mounting, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design systems that are robust to the mechanical stresses of Starship launch&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;General responsibilities:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in initial equipment conceptual development and carefully balance product specifications, requirements, layout complexity, cost, and lead-time limits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage electrical cabinet builds, field wiring, and conveyance installs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set, implement, and maintain schedules and budgets to ensure project completion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document control system built for handoff to pad operators&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in an engineering discipline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1+ years of experience in the design and commissioning of control systems for industrial applications (internship experience qualifies)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Electrical schematic CAD experience using EPLAN&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mechanical design experience with CAD, such as Siemens NX or SolidWorks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Field bus networks, serial communication, and Ethernet communication&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience building and commissioning high-quality electrical control panels and electro-mechanical systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of NEC, UL 508A codes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in fast-paced iterative design and test environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience solving complex problems with little to no supervision on schedule as an individual or as a member of an integrated team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong work ethic and drive to succeed as part of a high-functioning team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to rapidly change roles/responsibilities while working in a high-paced, challenging work environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to thrive in ambiguity, independently drive project progress, and manage multiple priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fundamental understanding of engineering principles behind electronic equipment, instrumentation, and commonly used industrial equipment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing and installing instrumentation and control systems in hazardous areas (National Fire Protection Association 70 (NFPA 70) Section 500 installations); Class 1, Division 1 and Division 2 environments or International Electrotechnical Commission (IEC) equivalence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with electrical power distribution, working knowledge of NFPA 70 and NFPA 70E&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with industrial bus protocols such as Modbus, Profinet, and EtherNet/IP&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be willing to work extended hours and/or weekends as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be willing to travel for extended periods, up to 100% during system activation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel to other SpaceX or third-party facilities (up to 20%)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to pass Air Force background checks for Cape Canaveral and Vandenberg&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stand: Up to 6 hours per day&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sit: Up to 6 hours per day&lt;/li&gt;
