&lt;p&gt;As part of the Raptor 3D printer team,&amp;nbsp;you will play&amp;nbsp;direct role in developing and scaling the printer and its production line. In this hands-on position, you will train technicians, create production plans and work instructions, collaborate with design and supply chain engineering, and design printer hardware, tooling, and shop aids. Working directly on the production floor, you will drive the rapid iteration and successful ramp of the Raptor 3D printer program. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solve complex, open-ended problems with an emphasis on speed of execution and efficiency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Refine the production system to create high-rate, high-yield, and reliable processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop training programs to teach engineers and technicians on laser tracking equipment and software&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use in-depth familiarity of GD&amp;amp;T to interpret blueprints at all assembly levels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effectively communicate with fabricators, machinists, assemblers, engineers, and other parties as required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the design, development, and implementation of custom production equipment for the Raptor 3D printer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Balance simultaneous projects of varying scope and complexity in a fast-paced environment&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
