&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of&amp;nbsp;enabling human life on Mars.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SOFTWARE ENGINEER – SIMULATION &amp;amp; FLIGHT SYSTEMS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Software Engineer in Special Programs, you’ll design, develop, and own critical software that powers the exploration and validation of next-generation technologies across every SpaceX flight system. You’ll take full ownership of new features in a scalable, high-performance application that spans the entire design–build–test–operations pipeline, while also contributing to critical control and flight system software. Your work will directly expand our capabilities in both ground and space systems and help prove out the innovations that make multiplanetary life possible.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a high-impact role where you’ll collaborate across engineering teams to build a high-throughput distributed system that develops and demonstrates cutting-edge software and hardware. The systems you create will be used by engineers pushing the limits of what’s possible—your code will help fly rockets, test vehicles, and shape the future of spaceflight.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Aerospace experience is not required. We’re looking for exceptionally smart, motivated software engineers who thrive on complex challenges, move fast in dynamic environments, and care deeply about software craftsmanship. Our software is mission-critical, and we have no shortage of hard, interesting problems that demand creative, high-quality solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Rapidly develop prototypes that prove key design concepts and quantify technical constraints&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop high-performance modules for real-time flight systems data streaming&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to test automation processes and CI/CD infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and maintain high-fidelity simulation and flight software for all vehicles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continually raise the bar for excellence through improving the reliability, performance, and scalability of our simulation and flight platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with engineers and customers to design and deliver new features that dramatically improve system capabilities and performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in computer science, engineering, math, or science discipline and 1+ years of experience in software development; or 3+ years of professional experience building software in lieu of a degree&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional experience with systems programming languages such as C++, Rust, or Go&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong software design and development skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with data streaming and real-time data processing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with data serialization formats such as JSON, YAML, XML, or Protobuf&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience delivering robust and scalable software applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Python, Java, or C#&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with containerized solutions such as Docker and Kubernetes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with relational databases (SQL, PostgreSQL, MySQL, or Oracle)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong skills in debugging, performance optimization, data throughput analysis, and unit testing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong creative and innovative problem-solving skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work effectively in a dynamic environment by quickly adapting to changing needs and requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Active Top Secret, Top Secret SCI, or DOE Level Q clearance, or the ability and willingness to obtain one&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This position requires successfully obtaining and maintaining a Top Secret Security Clearance as a condition of employment. While the clearance may not be immediately necessary upon hire, we encourage you to initiate the application process promptly upon accepting this offer. Your ability to secure the necessary clearance is essential for fulfilling key responsibilities of the role. Should you be unable to obtain it, SpaceX reserves the right to modify or terminate your employment to align with operational needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Note that an active clearance may provide the opportunity for you to work on sensitive SpaceX missions; if so, you will be subject to pre-employment drug and random drug and alcohol test&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to work extended hours and weekends when necessary to support proposal or critical project timelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
