&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of&amp;nbsp;enabling human life on Mars.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;INSIDER RISK ANALYST&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SpaceX is seeking a dynamic and driven individual with a demonstrated ability to work independently and as a member of a team in a fast-paced, high-tech environment. Our goal is to protect some of the world’s most advanced technologies including rockets, Dragon capsules for human transport, inter-planetary transport vehicles, the world&#39;s largest satellite communications network, etc. As an industry leader, we are a target of adversaries, both foreign and domestic, focused on slowing us down and accessing our proprietary technology. The work we do will literally safeguard mankind becoming an interplanetary species.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be responsible for the research, analysis, production, and dissemination of information relevant to protecting the safety and security of personnel, brand, global assets, intellectual property, and operations at SpaceX. This role will triage anomalous event data and analyze insider threat program datasets to respond to threats posed to SpaceX. You will use comprehensive understanding of various collection methods and platforms to explore new data sources, build effective queries, and combine information from disparate sources.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct comprehensive investigations and analysis in support of SpaceX intellectual property and security&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Uphold investigation and analytic tradecraft standards including confidentiality, objectivity, lawfulness, timeliness, and use of all available sources of information&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collect and analyze available program data to evaluate insider threat risk to SpaceX infrastructure, programs, and operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Triage anomalous event data associated with indicators of data exfiltration, data destruction and other key indicators of concern&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct internal investigations working with Information Security, HR, Legal, Government Security, Physical Security, and external partners based on information derived from internal and external sources&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Utilize network monitoring, data analytic, and other tools (DLP/SIEM/UEBA) to identify anomalous activity, initiate investigations and decipher underlying trends&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extract and organize insider threat program data to build metrics, reports and case studies addressing mission requirements and timelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate findings in a timely and accurate manner to team members, management, and relevant stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support employee training and briefings for internal and external audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Liaise with external industry and government partners to benchmark insider threat program, share threat intelligence, and further investigations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuously identify and help implement program improvement methods&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and safeguard sensitive information, including case files, employee PII, and intelligence reports&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree and 2+ years of professional experience in internal investigations, information security, or counterintelligence; OR 4+ years professional experience in information security, internal investigations, or counterintelligence in lieu of a degree&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1+ year using a SIEM and/or conducting digital forensic investigations in a government or corporate environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working level understanding of insider threat program missions, internal stakeholders, and manifestations of insider threats&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Microsoft Purview for eDiscovery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience performing business process automation or constructing data pipelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with risk-based alerting, detection, and tuning concepts for insider risk&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience conducting preliminary assessments, determining scope, investigation planning, evidence collection/handling, interviewing and reporting findings to internal and external stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to conduct interviews on short notice according to established internal guidelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and oral communication skills, with the ability to produce clear and concise reports&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly organized with a strong attention to detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to adapt to changing priorities and deadlines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Can swiftly adapt to new technical environments and workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to exercise discretion when conducting confidential investigations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
